ext explicitly states the cost of this distinction.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-042\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A cap can be raised\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text begins the cap increase section with this statement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-043\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text does not provide historical data on how many caps have been raised without measurement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-044\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The platform team looks at whether the load is smooth or bursty\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states this as part of the platform team's evaluation process.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-045\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a burst is cheaper to smooth than to serve at its peak.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text uses nearly identical language describing burst cost comparison.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-046\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A caller that can move half its work to a quieter hour usually gets what it needs without any change to the cap at all\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text provides this exact principle for managing capacity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-047\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Requests reach the platform team through the usual channel\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states this in the cap increase section.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-048\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n     