  },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-026\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a 503 means the platform itself is overloaded.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text provides this definition in the retry rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-027\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A client that folds all non-success responses into one branch will retry hardest during exactly the incident the cap was installed to survive.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states this principle about folding non-success responses.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-028\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A batch credential is allowed 1000 requests in a window\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states this allowance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-029\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"which is 50 times the default\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly provides this mathematical relationship.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-030\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A client written for one tier needs no change at all to run against the other. Nothing else about the two tiers differs.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The necessity that no client changes are needed entails the window, header and body are identical.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-031\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Nothing else about the two tiers differs.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states this about the batch tier.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-032\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A caller that cannot say how often it was refused cannot argue for a larger cap\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states inability to document refusals prevents cap increase arguments.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-033\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and nobody at the platform team will assemble that argument on its behalf.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states the team will not make the case for the caller.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-034\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The gateway refuses a request for three separate reasons\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states this count of separate reasons.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-035\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and only one of them is a cap.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states that one of three reasons is the cap.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-036\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text does not explicitly state which of the three reasons have no relation to traffic in the current window.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-037\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A credential may be suspended\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text lists credential suspension as a refusal reason.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-038\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a route may be closed for maintenance\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text mentions route closure during maintenance as a refusal reason.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-039\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text does not state that oversized bodies are refused before being read.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-040\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states this consequence of retrying against suspension.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-041\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"without ever reaching the service\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states this outcome of the retry loop.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-042\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the log afterwards shows nothing but a long run of refusals.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text describes the log as containing nothing but refusals.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-043\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text does not state whose budget is wasted in this scenario.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-044\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A caller that can move half its work to a quieter hour usually gets what it needs without any change to the cap at all\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text uses equivalent language about not needing cap changes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-045\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A cap can be raised\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states that caps can be raised.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-046\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A cap can be raised, but not without measurement behind the request.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text establishes that measurement is required for cap increases.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-047\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text does not specify the order in which the team evaluates load characteristics versus numbers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-048\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Requests reach the platform team through the usual channel\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states this routing for cap increase requests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-049\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"There is no expedited path\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states the absence of expedited processing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-050\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"are answered within two working days.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text specifies this response time for all cap increase requests.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":124235,"type":"result","duration_ms":189399,"uuid":"e08f4c72-0d90-4d99-b0f1-6bed32f10fb0","ttft_stream_ms":835,"time_to_request_ms":105,"first_content_frame_ms":836,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
